            <h2 class="p2-section-title">AC/DC dual-bus schematic — with transformer, rectifier, PWM</h2>
            <p class="p2-section-lead">
                The alternator produces raw AC. A full-wave bridge rectifier converts it to DC,
                filtered through a bulk capacitor, then a DC-DC buck converter regulates charge
                voltage into Battery B. Battery B feeds the PWM controller, which can trickle-top
                Battery A. Battery A powers the immersion heater element exclusively.
            </p>

